+"no probe A in the Librarian": "资料馆中没有样例 A",
+"no probe B in the Librarian": "资料馆中没有样例 B",
+"Onto the clipboard (in the lyrics, put it where the cursor stands)": "复制到剪贴板（在歌词中放到光标处）",
+"Onto the clipboard (in the lyrics, «[» offers it as you type)": "复制到剪贴板（在歌词中输入时“[”会提供它）",
+"into the Style prompt": "放入风格提示",
+"The prompt both probes were made with: into the Style prompt": "两个样例所用的提示：放入风格提示",
+"Voices": "嗓音",
+"Heard": "听感",
+"Families": "类别",
+"All families": "全部类别",
+"None of the 110 official examples writes it: YuE2 may sing it as words or pass it by": "110 个官方示例都没有写它：YuE2 可能把它当歌词唱出来或跳过",
+"the engine does not know the shofar: asked alone, it gives another horn": "引擎不认识羊角号：单独要求时会给出另一种号",
+"the engine plays a duduk; the adapter brings the recordings' reedy breath and phrasing": "引擎会演奏杜杜克；适配器带来录音中簧片的气息和乐句",
+"Sections (×: how often the 110 official examples write one; TEST: none does, Genius's guide to song sections names it)": "段落（×：110 个官方示例中写到的次数；测试：都没有写，Genius 的歌曲段落指南中提到）",
+"A section and how it is sung (after a dash or a colon)": "一个段落及其演唱方式（写在破折号或冒号之后）",
+"Who sings (no new section: the lines stay in the one before)": "谁来唱（不是新段落：这些句子仍属于前一段）",
+"What plays (an instrumental cue as a section)": "什么在演奏（作为段落的器乐提示）",
+"Meta-tags (one example of 110: their place is the Style prompt)": "元标签（110 个示例中仅 1 个：它们应放在风格提示中）",
+"The phonetic hand (Viktor's, from SUNO; YuE2 follows it as well)": "注音写法（Viktor 的，源自 SUNO；YuE2 也遵循）",
+"The body of the song: new words each time over the same music, the story moving on. Numbered (Verse 1, Verse 2…); the studio offers the next number.": "歌曲的主体：同样的音乐每次配新的歌词，故事向前推进。带编号（Verse 1、Verse 2…）；工作室会提供下一个编号。",
+"The part the song comes back to, the same words and melody each time, with the line people remember and sing along.": "歌曲反复回到的部分，每次歌词和旋律都相同，含有人们记住并跟唱的那一句。",
+"The climb from a verse into the chorus: a melody and words of its own that raise the tension, always followed by the chorus. Also written Prechorus.": "从主歌爬升到副歌：有自己的旋律和歌词来提升张力，后面总是接副歌。也写作 Prechorus。",
+"Once, late in the song, everything turns (melody, chords, words) before the song comes home to its chorus. The meter counts it with the verses.": "在歌曲后段出现一次，一切都转变（旋律、和弦、歌词），然后歌曲回到副歌。计数器把它和主歌一起计算。",
+"The ending: a last line repeated as the music fades, or the chorus once more with a change that resolves the song.": "结尾：音乐淡出时重复的最后一句，或再唱一遍副歌并加入使歌曲收束的变化。",
+"The opening before the first verse, mostly music. YuE2 seldom sings its lines: put a spoken intro under [Interlude] or [Verse].": "第一段主歌之前的开场，多为音乐。YuE2 很少唱这里的句子：说白开场请放在 [Interlude] 或 [Verse] 下。",
+"A passage of another feel between parts, often without words. Viktor's use: a pause in rap that brakes speech running ahead.": "各部分之间换一种感觉的段落，常常没有歌词。Viktor 的用法：说唱中的停顿，给抢拍的说词踩刹车。",
+"The last chorus, usually the biggest: more voices, more power, now and then a key change.": "最后一次副歌，通常最宏大：更多人声、更强力度，有时转调。",
+"The instruments alone between sections, for variety or to build into the next one. Name what plays: «Instrumental Break - Horns».": "段落之间只有乐器，用于变化或推向下一段。写明演奏什么：“Instrumental Break - Horns”。",
+"One instrument steps forward with a long melody of its own while the rest backs it. The examples also write Drum Solo, Keyboard Solo and plain Solo.": "一件乐器以自己的长旋律走到前面，其余伴奏。示例中也写作 Drum Solo、Keyboard Solo 或单写 Solo。",
+"The song's last mark: the music stops here. The examples also write Ends; SUNO's [END] is the same tag.": "歌曲的最后标记：音乐在此停止。示例中也写作 Ends；SUNO 的 [END] 是同一个标签。",
+"An opening played without voices. Also written Instrumental Introduction.": "不带人声演奏的开场。也写作 Instrumental Introduction。",
+"A line or two repeated unchanged at the end of each verse: part of the verse, not a section of its own as a chorus is.": "每段主歌结尾不变地重复的一两句：属于主歌的一部分，不像副歌那样是独立段落。",
+"A short part right after the chorus that carries its energy on (a chant, a riff, a tag line) before the next verse.": "紧接副歌之后的一小段，把副歌的能量延续到下一段主歌（口号、即兴乐句、点题句）。",
+"The music cut to its bones: heavy, simple riffs and pounding drums (metal and its kin), or a stripped beat in dance music.": "削到只剩骨架的音乐：沉重简单的连复段和重击的鼓（金属乐及其同类），或舞曲中精简的节拍。",
+"The music fades to silence. Also written Fadeout; Instrumental Fade Out once.": "音乐淡出至静音。也写作 Fadeout；有一次写作 Instrumental Fade Out。",
+"The catchiest line or riff of the song; Genius writes it [Chorus] or [Refrain] now.": "歌中最抓耳的一句或一段连复；Genius 现在写作 [Chorus] 或 [Refrain]。",
+"Dance and electronic music: the moment beat and bass hit after a build-up.": "舞曲和电子乐：铺垫之后节拍和贝斯砸下来的那一刻。",
+"A part, or a whole song, played without singing.": "不带演唱演奏的一部分，或整首歌。",
+"An ending played without voices.": "不带人声演奏的结尾。",
+"A short scene acted out apart from the song: voices and something happening, not singing.": "在歌曲之外表演的一小段场景：人声和情节，不是演唱。",
+"A spoken or played passage that joins two songs within one track.": "在同一条音轨中连接两首歌的说白或演奏段落。",
+"One of the songs a long track is made of, numbered in Roman numerals (Part I, Part II); the verses keep counting across the parts.": "一条长音轨由若干首歌组成，其中之一，用罗马数字编号（Part I、Part II）；主歌编号跨部分连续。",
+"Wordless syllables sung like an instrument, as in jazz.": "像乐器一样唱出的无词音节，如爵士乐中那样。",
+"Quick leaps between chest and head voice, as in an alpine yodel.": "在胸声与头声之间快速跳跃，如阿尔卑斯约德尔调。",
+"Voices without words: oohs, aahs, hums, a vocalise.": "无词的人声：哦、啊、哼鸣、元音吟唱。",
+"Verse 1 – Her": "Verse 1 – Her",
+"Vocal ad-libs": "即兴人声",
+"MOOD, TEMPO, INSTRUMENTATION, ARRANGEMENT, PRODUCTION, STRUCTURE, DYNAMICS, EMOTIONS too": "MOOD、TEMPO、INSTRUMENTATION、ARRANGEMENT、PRODUCTION、STRUCTURE、DYNAMICS，还有 EMOTIONS",
+"a stress mark after a vowel: обе́щано, сули́т (holds in more than 95 % of lines)": "元音之后的重音符：обе́щано、сули́т（在超过 95 % 的句子中有效）",
+"a capital stressed vowel pushes the stress where the rhyme wants it: базилиО́": "大写的重读元音把重音推到押韵需要的位置：базилиО́",
+"ע inside a Russian word sings a soft о/а: кעмо́рка, пעле́но; it also brakes rap that runs ahead": "俄语单词中的 ע 唱成柔和的 о/а：кעмо́рка、пעле́но；它也能给抢拍的说唱踩刹车",
+"a Latin o inside a Russian word sings a hard, open o where the model would say а: Кo дну": "俄语单词中的拉丁字母 o 在模型会说 а 的地方唱成硬而开的 o：Кo дну",
+"a stretched vowel holds a note: where the music has room for it, not on every line": "拉长的元音会撑住一个音：在音乐留有空间的地方，而不是每一句",
